					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "RESIZE\n\nThe Resize node allows you to resize your texture.\nThe node has multiple modes that each resize the texture in their own ways (stretch, fit, fill).\n\nBy default Resize will use linear sampling, but this can be disabled in the node panel.\n\nThe Resolution can be set to either absolute or relative.\n\nIn absolute mode you set exactly how many pixels you want.\nIn relative mode (default) you set a factor to which the texture is scaled in relation patch resolution."
					}
				},
